  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Javed Shaikh vs State Of Maharashtra on 31 January, 2024 Author: G. S. Kulkarni Bench: G. S. Kulkarni 914.Wpl3364_ Vidya Amin In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Ordinary Original Civil Jurisdiction Writ Petition (L) No. 3364 Of 2024 Javed Shaikh ... Petitioner Versus State of Maharashtra & Ors. ...Respondents None for the petitioner.",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "The petitioner, who is a resident in the vicinity of Chansawali Dargah, Niti Road, Powai, Andheri (East), Mumbai is before the Court in the present proceedings, making a grievance in regard to what he alleges as an illegal setup of \"a fair\" which is not limited to stalls but also having huge high raised swings, giant wheel etc. which are stated to be installed at the risk of life of the citizens residing in the vicinity thereby infringing their rights guaranteed under Article 21 of the Constitution of India. 2. The petitioner has stated that the Municipal Corporation of Greater Mumbai has issued a Circular dated 2 November, 2015 prescribing conditions in issuing permission to a fair/live events, which is not limited to obtaining permission of the said authority, but requiring the concerned persons involved in conducting/participating in such fairs to file separate applications for NOC 31 January, 2024 914.WPL3364_2024.DOC to be obtained from various departments like health department and other authorities, necessary for organizing a fair/live event."
  },
